  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1213 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nA drying trend commences on Monday though southern and eastern\nareas will see one more round of heavy rain producing\nthunderstorms. A few strong storms will be possible across the \nplains where shears will range from 25 to 35 kts in the \nafternoon. Flash Flooding of Aspen Acres burn scar still looks \npossible though thunderstorm coverage may be a little less which\nmay reduce the risk some. \n\nThe upper high expands westward for Tuesday then amplifies\nacross the western U.S. through mid week as a shortwave trough\npasses by to the north and east on Wednesday. Hot temperatures \nand mostly dry conditions will return for Tuesday with highs \nrebounding into the mid to upper 90s across the plains. A cold \nfront brings another uptick in thunderstorms to the southeast \nmountains and plains Wednesday and possibly Thursday. With \nsoutheasterly low level flow beneath northwest flow aloft, shear\nwill be sufficient for strong to severe thunderstorms as long \nas low level moisture and sufficient CAPE is maintained. There \nis some drying coming in from the north on Thursday which could \nshunt the strong to severe storm potential to south of highway \n50 on Thursday. \n\nOtherwise...warmer weather returns for Friday into the weekend\nwith a southerly moisture tap out west recirculating through \nthe upper high bringing another gradual moistening along with \nincreasing thunderstorm chances across the mountains next \nweekend. -KT",
